<!-- livebook:{"chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.Spiral.Cells.SmartCell","attrs":{"timeout":300,"source":":= article () : page.entry =\n    {\n        slug = \"showcase\"\n        title = \"Every Block, Once\"\n        date = \"2026-10-18\"\n        kind = page.Article\n        authors = [ { name = \"i574n\"; handle = \"i574n\" } ]\n        blurb = \"A sample post that renders every block the blog engine has.\"\n        blocks =\n            [\n                post.Paragraph (\n                    \"This post exercises the engine: every block kind appears at least once, and a test fails when \"\n                    ^^ \"one is missing.\"\n                )\n                post.Heading \"Text\"\n                post.Paragraph \"Paragraphs escape their text, so <tags> & ampersands print as written.\"\n                post.Note \"A note renders as an aside.\"\n                post.Heading \"Code\"\n                post.Code (\"spiral\", \"inl twice f x = f (f x)\\ntwice ((+) 1i32) 40i32\")\n                post.Terminal (\"pwsh scripts/build.ps1\", \"BLOG-OK blog/engine\")\n                post.Heading \"Data\"\n                post.Table (\n                    [ \"Block\"; \"Renders as\" ],\n                    [\n                        [ \"Heading\"; \"an h2 with a section anchor and a table of contents entry\" ]\n                        [ \"Table\"; \"a table with a head row and escaped cells\" ]\n                    ]\n                )\n                post.Rule\n                post.Heading \"Conclusion\"\n                post.Paragraph \"Real posts live in the repositories they describe; this one only shows the machinery.\"\n            ]\n    }\n\n:= release () : page.entry =\n    := a = article ()\n    { a ?|\n        slug = \"showcase-release\"\n        title = \"Engine Release Notes\"\n        kind = page.Release\n        blurb = \"A sample release entry, so the Releases tab has content.\"\n        blocks = [ post.Paragraph \"Release entries share the article layout and get a Release label in the index.\" ]\n    }\n\n:= entries () : list page.entry =\n    [ article (); release () ]\n\n:= block_tag (b : post.block) : string =\n    ?= b ?|\n    | post.Heading _ => \"heading\"\n    | post.Paragraph _ => \"paragraph\"\n    | post.Code _ => \"code\"\n    | post.Terminal _ => \"terminal\"\n    | post.Table _ => \"table\"\n    | post.Note _ => \"note\"\n    | post.Rule => \"rule\"\n\n:= ^ tags (blocks : list post.block) : string =\n    ?= blocks ?|\n    | [] => \"\"\n    | b :: rest => \" \" ++# block_tag b ++# tags rest\n\n:= ^ all_present (present : string) (wanted : list string) : bool =\n    ?= wanted ?|\n    | [] => !+\n    | t :: rest => (present |> sm'.contains (\" \" ++# t)) && all_present present rest","print_code":false},"livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Spiral.Cells.eval!(
  ~S"""
  := article () : page.entry =
      {
          slug = "showcase"
          title = "Every Block, Once"
          date = "2026-10-18"
          kind = page.Article
          authors = [ { name = "i574n"; handle = "i574n" } ]
          blurb = "A sample post that renders every block the blog engine has."
          blocks =
              [
                  post.Paragraph (
                      "This post exercises the engine: every block kind appears at least once, and a test fails when "
                      ^^ "one is missing."
                  )
                  post.Heading "Text"
                  post.Paragraph "Paragraphs escape their text, so <tags> & ampersands print as written."
                  post.Note "A note renders as an aside."
                  post.Heading "Code"
                  post.Code ("spiral", "inl twice f x = f (f x)\ntwice ((+) 1i32) 40i32")
                  post.Terminal ("pwsh scripts/build.ps1", "BLOG-OK blog/engine")
                  post.Heading "Data"
                  post.Table (
                      [ "Block"; "Renders as" ],
                      [
                          [ "Heading"; "an h2 with a section anchor and a table of contents entry" ]
                          [ "Table"; "a table with a head row and escaped cells" ]
                      ]
                  )
                  post.Rule
                  post.Heading "Conclusion"
                  post.Paragraph "Real posts live in the repositories they describe; this one only shows the machinery."
              ]
      }

  := release () : page.entry =
      := a = article ()
      { a ?|
          slug = "showcase-release"
          title = "Engine Release Notes"
          kind = page.Release
          blurb = "A sample release entry, so the Releases tab has content."
          blocks = [ post.Paragraph "Release entries share the article layout and get a Release label in the index." ]
      }

  := entries () : list page.entry =
      [ article (); release () ]

  := block_tag (b : post.block) : string =
      ?= b ?|
      | post.Heading _ => "heading"
      | post.Paragraph _ => "paragraph"
      | post.Code _ => "code"
      | post.Terminal _ => "terminal"
      | post.Table _ => "table"
      | post.Note _ => "note"
      | post.Rule => "rule"

  := ^ tags (blocks : list post.block) : string =
      ?= blocks ?|
      | [] => ""
      | b :: rest => " " ++# block_tag b ++# tags rest

  := ^ all_present (present : string) (wanted : list string) : bool =
      ?= wanted ?|
      | [] => !+
      | t :: rest => (present |> sm'.contains (" " ++# t)) && all_present present rest
  """,
  timeout: 300_000
)
```

#### every_block_kind_appears (test)

<!-- livebook:{"chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.Spiral.Cells.SmartCell","attrs":{"timeout":300,"source":"///- --test\n\n:= a = article ()\nall_present (tags a.blocks) [ \"heading\"; \"paragraph\"; \"code\"; \"terminal\"; \"table\"; \"note\"; \"rule\" ]\n|> _assert_eq !+","print_code":false},"livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Spiral.Cells.eval!(
  ~S"""
  ///- --test

  := a = article ()
  all_present (tags a.blocks) [ "heading"; "paragraph"; "code"; "terminal"; "table"; "note"; "rule" ]
  |> _assert_eq !+
  """,
  timeout: 300_000
)
```

